cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use ParallaX, please cite it using the metadata in this file, and
  cite the SPHEREx data and the NASA/IPAC Infrared Science Archive as described
  in the README.
type: software
title: "ParallaX: chromatic difference imaging for the SPHEREx sky"
abstract: >-
  ParallaX is a web tool and Python pipeline that plays SPHEREx Level-2
  spectral images of any patch of sky as a time sequence. Because every SPHEREx
  exposure has its own per-pixel wavelength, it predicts the static sky at each
  frame's wavelengths from the other survey passes (a chromatic template),
  subtracts it, and reports a reproducible three-way comparison with naive and
  wavelength-gated pair differencing, including injection-recovery tests on
  real frames. Entry of team ZENITH LABS to the NASA Space Apps Challenge 2026,
  challenge "Planet X and SPHEREx". Not affiliated with or endorsed by NASA.
